From ef42ab9813a7414bbc0888bab8e4e86cec098b31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 12:29:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix critical UI/UX bugs and add mobile navigation, scroll
 animations

Fixes found via full audit + browser testing (Playwright screenshots
at desktop and mobile viewports):

Critical rendering bugs:
- Hero CTA buttons were invisible (transparent bg, no text color) due
  to a later duplicate CSS rule referencing undefined variables
  (--secondary/--white/--primary) that silently won the cascade
- 12+ undefined CSS custom properties (--bg-surface, --glass-bg,
  --transition-normal, --primary, --secondary, --white, etc.) broke
  section backgrounds across #repository, #research, framework cards,
  research cards and more; added proper aliases in variables.css
- White-on-white / dark-on-dark text contrast bugs in the Global
  Coverage region cards, global stat pills and research cards
- Missing closing </div> in the hero collapsed the two-column layout,
  pushing the world map card below the fold instead of beside the text
- World map image file was PNG binary data saved with a .svg
  extension, so it failed to render; renamed to .png and fixed src
- #dashboard-gallery had zero padding/background because the CSS only
  targeted #dashboard (an ID that doesn't match); dashboard image,
  region pill, status badge and edition tag were entirely unstyled
- Global Market Intelligence dashboard-gallery section, architecture
  card badges (8 of 9 cards were missing them), and section eyebrow
  labels (.section-kicker) had no styles at all
- Removed duplicated/orphaned stat boxes sitting outside the
  .global-metrics grid, a dead #dashboards footer anchor, and a stray
  stray "0" typo in the footer copyright line

UX additions:
- Mobile navigation: hamburger menu, off-canvas panel, was completely
  absent before (header.css had zero @media queries)
- Responsive hero: two-column grid now stacks on mobile, heading uses
  clamp() instead of a fixed 68px size, brand/tagline truncate instead
  of overflowing the header on small screens
- Scroll-reveal animations, active nav-link highlighting on scroll,
  sticky header state, animated stat counters, skip-to-content link,
  focus-visible states, custom scrollbar/selection color

Verified with Playwright screenshots at 1440px and 390px viewports
before committing.
